WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.077
Step three is the guide's
monthly evidence run,

2
00:00:03.077 --> 00:00:06.025
shortened on the slide;
the page has it in full.

3
00:00:06.025 --> 00:00:11.275
Use a new, empty evidence folder,
because the run hashes every file in it.

4
00:00:11.275 --> 00:00:15.120
It connects, runs the three
read-only queries for coverage,

5
00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.525
Attack Surface Reduction and
prevention, and writes each to a file.

6
00:00:19.525 --> 00:00:24.643
It exports the last thirty days of incidents,
filtered on the created date time,

7
00:00:24.643 --> 00:00:27.477
which Microsoft Learn lists as filterable,

8
00:00:27.477 --> 00:00:31.650
with their severity, status,
classification and determination.

9
00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:35.525
Then it hashes every file in
the folder into a checksum file.

10
00:00:35.525 --> 00:00:37.621
You should see the coverage, A S R,

11
00:00:37.621 --> 00:00:41.250
prevention and incidents
files, and the checksum file.

12
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:45.838
Step four checks the hashes, the way
next month's run checks last month's.

13
00:00:45.838 --> 00:00:49.830
It reads the checksum file, leaves
out the checksum file's own entry,

14
00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:52.733
since the run writes it
into the folder it hashes,

15
00:00:52.733 --> 00:00:55.637
and compares each recorded
hash with a fresh one.

16
00:00:55.637 --> 00:00:58.463
Matches should be true
for every evidence file.

17
00:00:58.463 --> 00:01:01.087
False means a file changed
after it was filed.

18
00:01:01.087 --> 00:01:05.660
Step five backs it out: nothing
changed in the tenant, so disconnect.
